[TITLE] Self-monitoring of an isolated power station
[P1] On a hard-to-reach shelf, a station feeds a dispensary. It's a radio relay. The micro-grid includes solar panels, lithium batteries and a small diesel generator. Since the road can remain closed for days, a controller measures the voltage, the current. temperature and vibrations every 200 milliseconds. Detailed data remains in place; only a compressed summary is transmitted when the link is operational Medical and communication equipment is a priority
[P2] It's the 18th of October 2025. A dust storm reduced solar output by 34% in 15 minutes. The temperature of the battery compartment has risen by 8°C. While the inverter fan was producing an abnormal vibration. Instead of shutting down the station, the system turned off the secondary heating, reduced some of the lights, and started the rescue group. It identified three possible causes of the debris on the panels, a worn-out bearing, and increasing resistance in a battery connector.
[P3] After the storm, a head-mounted camera read the license plates and alarm codes. And then a local processor compared them to the offline manual. No sensitive images were sent to the cloud. The software required that the entire label remain within a safe margin, and it also controlled the overall sharpness and that of the upper part. A sound signal was given to back up if a edge was missing, and four steady frames were needed. The engineers then confirmed the proposed order to clean the panels, replace the bearing, and then tighten the connector. The intervention lasted six minutes without interrupting a critical service reliable automation must recognize uncertainty and leave the final decision to the operator
